course: dictionary
lesson: 13906
title: Sideways and clever
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Laterally means sideways, or to the side. The word comes from «lateral», which is about the side of something. «The crab walked laterally across the rock pool.» The crab did not go forward or back. It moved to the side, so laterally means sideways.
explain: Try the swap check: put «sideways» in place of «laterally» and see if the sentence still makes sense. «The crab walked sideways across the rock pool.» It does, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Laterally can also describe thinking. To think laterally is to solve a problem in an unusual, creative way instead of the obvious one. «Maya could not open the box, so she thought laterally and used a hairclip instead of the key.» She did not look for the obvious answer. She tried a new, clever idea.
fact: Laterally means sideways, or to the side.
fact: «Lateral» is the adjective, and «laterally» is the adverb that tells you how something moves or is done.
fact: To think laterally is to find an unusual, creative answer instead of the obvious one.
fact: In sport, a player may pass the ball laterally, which means across the pitch and not forward.
fact: Lateral thinking puzzles often have clever, unexpected answers, so look for the idea nobody expected.
exercise: «The crab walked laterally across the rock pool.» What does laterally mean here? | Under the water | Backwards | *Sideways | Very fast
exercise: «Maya was stuck on the puzzle, so she thought laterally and tried an unexpected idea.» What does thinking laterally mean? | Copying the obvious answer | Thinking very slowly | Going to sleep | *Finding a clever, unusual answer
exercise: Copy the one word that means to the side. | *laterally | ball | dog | stepped
test: «The footballer passed the ball laterally to her teammate.» Where did the ball go? | Up into the air | Back to the goalkeeper | *Across, to the side | Forward into the goal
test: «Sam was stuck on the riddle, so he thought laterally and found a surprising answer.» Which is the best meaning of thought laterally? | Copied a friend's answer | Read the riddle very slowly | *Solved it in an unusual, creative way | Gave up at once
exam: «The scientist saw that the beetle could move laterally, but not straight ahead.» Which word best matches laterally? | Upwards | *Sideways | Backwards | Quietly
